# Vercel CLI project linkage. Not secret, but it is local machine
# state and has no business in the repository.
.vercel

# Supabase CLI machine state: CLI/Postgres versions, pooler URL, and WHICH
# PROJECT this checkout is linked to. Committing it makes "am I linked to
# staging or production" shared state, which is how a branch ends up carrying
# a staging link into main. Nothing in the build, deploy or test path reads
# it: Vercel builds with VITE_ env vars, not CLI linkage, and a production
# build that named the wrong project would be failed by
# scripts/check-release-env.mjs regardless.
supabase/.temp

# Local speech-to-text proof of concept: virtual environment and model weights.
# `python -m venv` writes its own `.gitignore` containing `*`, so the venv is
# already ignored -- but that protection lives INSIDE the venv and disappears
# if the directory is ever recreated by other means. The rule is stated here
# too, because a single NCAIR1/Yoruba-ASR checkout is ~926 MiB and a repository
# does not recover from that being committed.
#
# Model caches are kept OUTSIDE the repository (the default HF_HOME under the
# user profile), which is the real guarantee; these patterns only cover the
# case where someone points HF_HOME at the working tree.
.venv-stt/
.venv/
venv/
models--*/
*.safetensors
*.ckpt

# The built backend bundle. Rebuilt by `npm run build:server` on every
# deploy, so committing it would only create merge conflicts and a stale
# artefact that looks authoritative.
dist-server/

# Python caches and local backup files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.bak

# Private credentials and local sessions
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.test.example
/scripts/TEST-LOGINS.md
.wwebjs_auth/
auth_info_baileys/
session/
